WEBVTT

00:45.128 --> 00:46.671
PATIENT NAME
LEE MYUNG-HAN

00:48.089 --> 00:50.467
There's an arrest warrant out
for Mr. Lee Myung-han.

00:50.550 --> 00:53.053
Charges are extortion and insurance fraud.

01:16.284 --> 01:18.161
He's in his room right now.

01:18.244 --> 01:20.080
A biopsy found he has…

01:21.623 --> 01:22.707
lung cancer.

01:23.583 --> 01:26.127
They like to run
more tests tomorrow.

01:27.712 --> 01:31.091
If you still have to take him in,
do what you have to do.

01:39.891 --> 01:41.184
Ugh, what a headache.

01:41.893 --> 01:43.728
- Constable Kim.
- Yes, sir?

01:43.812 --> 01:46.940
Go talk to, uh, whoever doctor's on call.
Find out if we can arrest him

01:47.023 --> 01:48.983
- or if we'll have to wait.
- Yes, sir.

01:49.067 --> 01:49.901
Mm-hm.

01:52.570 --> 01:54.239
ULTRASOUND ROOM

01:55.865 --> 01:57.909
Miss Chae Yu-jin's guardian can come in.

01:57.992 --> 01:59.619
- Yes?
- We're ready for you.

01:59.702 --> 02:00.745
Oh.

02:01.621 --> 02:05.375
So, your stomach is tightening.

02:05.458 --> 02:07.627
It's really quite common.

02:07.710 --> 02:11.005
As your uterus is expanding
to make space for the baby.

02:11.840 --> 02:15.301
Thankfully,
your baby's absolutely perfect.

02:20.140 --> 02:21.307
And let's see.

02:21.891 --> 02:24.310
I'll find the heartbeat for you, too.

02:54.674 --> 02:57.552
Sometimes,
choices that seem so obvious

02:57.635 --> 03:00.471
suddenly change
and become impossible to make.

03:15.862 --> 03:18.615
When you can't do
what you think you need to,

03:19.115 --> 03:21.034
there's no way to go forward.

03:22.035 --> 03:23.578
But you can't go back, either.

03:38.843 --> 03:40.803
The officers left.

03:40.887 --> 03:43.014
They need the doctors to sign off,

03:43.848 --> 03:46.267
and he won't
until the testing is complete.

03:50.271 --> 03:51.314
So…

03:52.190 --> 03:54.984
were you able to talk to your dad at all?

03:59.864 --> 04:01.449
Si-woo, are you crying?

04:05.411 --> 04:07.372
I'm okay. I just need space.

04:11.292 --> 04:13.795
Anyway, we're not in the office,
we don't have to pretend.

04:16.631 --> 04:18.800
You don't need to act like you care
how I'm doing.

04:20.009 --> 04:21.010
Director.

04:29.852 --> 04:32.063
Even if we're not sure

04:32.146 --> 04:36.359
which choice is right
or which will do the least damage,

04:36.442 --> 04:39.362
we still have to decide, to make a choice.

04:39.988 --> 04:41.906
We try to do what is right

04:42.865 --> 04:46.160
to live up to the right expectations.

04:46.786 --> 04:47.996
THIS SPRING

04:48.079 --> 04:49.122
Here.

04:51.207 --> 04:52.667
How's work?

04:53.835 --> 04:55.920
Sir, what's your secret? How do you do it?

04:57.130 --> 04:59.382
Hm? My secret?

04:59.465 --> 05:03.011
Your forecast are the most accurate
statistically in all of the KMA.

05:03.094 --> 05:04.846
No one else even comes close.

05:04.929 --> 05:07.724
You… You're a living legend, really.

05:07.807 --> 05:09.809
You've made history.
So, how do you get it right?

05:10.393 --> 05:12.145
Hmm…

05:12.228 --> 05:14.564
Sounds like you should be
trying harder, hm?

05:14.647 --> 05:17.567
I set the record ages ago,
and no one's come close?

05:17.650 --> 05:18.609
That's just sad.

05:18.693 --> 05:21.362
You could tell me your secret
to getting it right,

05:21.446 --> 05:23.406
then see if I can break your record.

05:23.489 --> 05:24.449
Huh?

05:25.241 --> 05:27.577
What do you think? Do you wanna know?

05:28.286 --> 05:30.538
Yes. I'd really like to know.

05:30.621 --> 05:31.914
Would you tell me, sir?

05:33.166 --> 05:34.792
Okay, then.

05:34.876 --> 05:36.669
You'll find out if you figure out

05:36.753 --> 05:39.088
who has the worst forecast history
at the KMA.

05:39.922 --> 05:40.757
What?

05:43.051 --> 05:45.053
Figure that mystery out,
and you'll know my secret.

05:45.136 --> 05:46.220
Okay?

05:50.308 --> 05:57.065
EPISODE 16
TOMORROW'S ANSWERS

05:57.148 --> 05:59.108
FINALE

06:16.459 --> 06:17.543
You're late.

06:18.378 --> 06:24.801
Oh, well, they change the forecast
and I had to smooth things over.

06:28.888 --> 06:29.722
Sorry.

06:33.017 --> 06:35.103
You must be tired. Get some sleep.

06:36.270 --> 06:37.313
Hyang-rae.

06:41.692 --> 06:42.777
What?

06:45.154 --> 06:47.031
Should… Should we divorce each other?

06:48.324 --> 06:49.242
What?

06:51.369 --> 06:54.247
I was just thinking on my way coming here,

06:55.873 --> 06:57.917
what Bo-mi wanted was so sad to me.

06:58.000 --> 07:00.002
All she asked for was a dinner

07:00.086 --> 07:02.505
where we would go out on her birthday
and eat together.

07:03.965 --> 07:08.970
And even then, I'm so pathetic
that I can't manage one dinner.

07:13.099 --> 07:15.309
That might be the best that I can do.

07:39.750 --> 07:40.710
All right.

07:43.087 --> 07:46.716
- What do your parents do for a living?
- Huh?

07:46.799 --> 07:48.384
You're doing it again, Eomma.

07:50.720 --> 07:53.097
Both my parents worked as teachers
when I was a kid.

07:53.723 --> 07:57.393
My father thought high school physics
and retired two years ago.

07:57.477 --> 07:59.937
My mother is still working.
She's a vice-principal now.

08:00.563 --> 08:04.192
Oh, so education runs in your family.

08:04.275 --> 08:05.485
Tell me about yourself.

08:05.568 --> 08:07.570
Where did you get your degree?

08:07.653 --> 08:09.655
I majored in physics at Hanguk University.

08:09.739 --> 08:12.867
Oh, Ha-kyung went to that school.
Did you know that?

08:12.950 --> 08:14.994
Yes. I was way before her, though.

08:15.077 --> 08:16.329
Oh.

08:17.288 --> 08:19.624
And this apartment…

08:19.707 --> 08:20.875
I own it.

08:20.958 --> 08:24.545
Uh, I haven't completely paid off
the mortgage yet,

08:24.629 --> 08:26.130
but it… it's in my name.

08:27.048 --> 08:32.178
I know that your work is fairly stable.
You own this place, so you're ready.

08:32.261 --> 08:33.721
All that's left is the wedding.

08:33.804 --> 08:36.891
- Huh?
- Ah, Mom! Mom, don't say things like that.

08:37.475 --> 08:40.061
You always go way too fast.
You'll scare him away.

08:40.144 --> 08:42.897
- Oh, I wouldn't say that.
- I'm sorry, Mr. Shin.

08:42.980 --> 08:45.107
Don't worry about anything.
She does this all the time.

08:45.191 --> 08:47.902
Marriage is all
she ever wants to talk about.

08:47.985 --> 08:50.404
That's why Ha-kyung moved out
to live on her own.

08:51.072 --> 08:54.575
Well, there's, um, expectation
that you'll get married one day, right?

08:54.659 --> 08:56.619
No way.

09:00.206 --> 09:03.459
We aren't expecting it?
Not even in the future?

09:03.543 --> 09:07.213
We… We weren't even close to that stuff.

09:11.300 --> 09:13.135
Then why did you sleep with me?

09:14.136 --> 09:17.056
When two people date
and it goes well, they do that.

09:18.266 --> 09:23.312
It's not what we were doing.
We were just sleeping together. Right?

09:23.396 --> 09:26.065
You and me, it was a real thing, yeah?

09:26.732 --> 09:28.818
We connected together, didn't we?

09:28.901 --> 09:32.863
And we felt, uh… love. Beyond that, we…

09:32.947 --> 09:34.907
It wasn't just physical for us.

09:34.991 --> 09:36.993
No, no, no. Hey, hey. Stop it, stop it.

09:37.076 --> 09:40.496
This is something for you two
to figure out privately.

09:40.580 --> 09:41.872
I thought…

09:43.416 --> 09:45.001
You are my first…

09:45.084 --> 09:46.711
First one. And I…

09:46.794 --> 09:50.756
Jin Tae-kyung, you are my first love,
you are my first everything.

09:50.840 --> 09:52.133
Oh.

09:52.216 --> 09:53.551
Well, well, so what?

09:53.634 --> 09:55.219
I'm responsible for you now?

09:55.303 --> 09:56.762
I'll go. I've heard enough.

09:56.846 --> 09:59.181
Were you playing with me?
I'm a toy to you?

09:59.265 --> 10:00.725
The fact that you'd even say that!

10:00.808 --> 10:02.226
I'm not that kind of girl!

10:02.310 --> 10:04.395
You were just gonna go all the way
with someone you didn't wanna marry?

10:04.478 --> 10:06.314
I liked you. I do like you.

10:06.397 --> 10:08.441
That's why we dated,
and why we went all the way!

10:08.524 --> 10:09.442
- I can't believe this.
- I'm sick here.

10:09.525 --> 10:11.611
I thought you liked me
and you were serious!

10:11.694 --> 10:12.987
I do like you!

10:13.070 --> 10:15.865
- But you said you don't want to marry me.
- That's right. I don't want to!

10:15.948 --> 10:17.116
It doesn't…

10:17.199 --> 10:19.452
Oh, jeez!

10:26.292 --> 10:29.712
Gusts of cold wind are
bringing down temperatures even further.

10:29.795 --> 10:32.882
Right now, let's take a look at Seoul.
Currently, 3 degrees Celcius.

10:32.965 --> 10:35.176
This evening, we'll see things deep
below freezing.

10:35.259 --> 10:37.928
Thankfully, it will rise back
above zero tomorrow morning.

10:38.012 --> 10:39.722
We'll get that warm weather back.

10:47.229 --> 10:48.230
Yu-jin.

10:48.314 --> 10:50.733
- Hm?
- I remembered it.

10:51.525 --> 10:52.401
What?

10:52.485 --> 10:55.279
The exact day, the very moment
I started loving you.

11:03.704 --> 11:04.747
Excuse me.

11:05.247 --> 11:07.124
What's an area of dense temperature?

11:08.626 --> 11:10.252
There was a part of the briefing.

11:10.336 --> 11:13.631
Oh, it was talking about the warm air
being introduced to the west coast.

11:14.799 --> 11:17.343
It's where the isothermal lines
are concentrated.

11:17.968 --> 11:19.845
Oh, that makes sense.

11:22.139 --> 11:25.976
Okay, what about the relationship between
the vertical structure of temperature

11:26.060 --> 11:27.311
and the water equivalent?

11:27.395 --> 11:29.855
I wasn't able to find it. Could you…

11:31.273 --> 11:34.860
The vertical structure has information
like vertical temperature

11:34.944 --> 11:36.362
and humidity of a certain area.

11:37.279 --> 11:38.406
And so…

11:38.906 --> 11:42.076
You fell in love with me
and thought I was an idiot?

11:42.660 --> 11:43.703
No.

11:43.786 --> 11:44.912
Then what?

11:44.995 --> 11:47.164
It was just the way
you looked at me that day.

11:51.043 --> 11:53.754
If you look here, you can see
if the numerical development

11:53.838 --> 11:55.131
is gonna be strong or not.

11:55.214 --> 11:57.800
And whether the structure
is one where the water content

11:57.883 --> 12:00.177
will allow the snowflakes to grow.

12:05.015 --> 12:07.309
You looked at me
in this way that…

12:07.393 --> 12:08.436
Oh.

12:10.688 --> 12:13.566
…made me feel like
I could do anything if you were there.

12:20.489 --> 12:21.699
In that moment,

12:22.533 --> 12:25.244
I felt like I was doing everything
I should be doing.

12:27.037 --> 12:29.540
I could tell. I could see it in your eyes.

12:30.875 --> 12:34.378
"Wow, there isn't anything
he doesn't know."

12:34.962 --> 12:37.173
"He's such an expert,
I could ask him anything,

12:37.256 --> 12:38.966
well, about weather."

12:39.049 --> 12:42.511
"And he doesn't talk down
to anyone with a question."

12:43.137 --> 12:43.971
"What a stud."

12:46.599 --> 12:47.850
That's how I felt.

12:51.562 --> 12:52.938
Could you believe in me

12:54.482 --> 12:56.817
in that way about things today?

12:59.779 --> 13:02.531
It's not enough,
'cause it's about reality.

13:03.699 --> 13:05.367
A kid isn't something to do, just 'cause…

13:06.744 --> 13:07.703
I know.

13:08.287 --> 13:10.664
You should see
my search history this week.

13:11.499 --> 13:14.460
- Kids are really expensive.
- I know that, too.

13:15.044 --> 13:16.879
It's not just us, though.

13:16.962 --> 13:18.964
Everyone has to deal with this.

13:19.048 --> 13:21.884
They all have kids anyway,
and they all seem just fine.

13:21.967 --> 13:23.761
Why shouldn't we do it, too?

13:26.430 --> 13:27.723
Honestly, Yu-jin,

13:29.183 --> 13:31.977
when we heard the heartbeat yesterday,

13:32.603 --> 13:34.563
my heart could've burst out of my chest.

13:36.524 --> 13:39.902
It felt like the first time
our kid was talking to the two of us.

13:42.488 --> 13:43.823
Saying that it's here.

13:45.032 --> 13:46.200
That it exists.

13:49.036 --> 13:52.081
And I felt like I wanted to say something.

13:55.000 --> 13:56.418
"That's right, kid."

13:57.378 --> 13:58.379
"Hello."

14:00.339 --> 14:01.924
"This is your dad speaking."

14:16.856 --> 14:17.690
Yu-jin.

14:18.440 --> 14:19.984
I will do better

14:20.484 --> 14:22.903
for you and our kid's sake.

14:26.198 --> 14:27.157
Hm?

14:38.586 --> 14:39.837
Thank you.

14:48.095 --> 14:49.471
I love you.

14:52.641 --> 14:53.934
I love you too.

14:58.439 --> 14:59.773
You too.

15:12.036 --> 15:15.039
I'm gonna be a father now. Got to provide.

15:15.122 --> 15:17.875
So get it together and do
what you've got to do.

15:20.210 --> 15:22.755
PENSION CREDIT APPLICATION FORM
FOR CIVIL SERVANTS

15:23.881 --> 15:26.425
- You're sure about this?
- What?

15:26.508 --> 15:29.303
When you take out pension credit,
you're using the money

15:29.386 --> 15:32.848
for your retirement in advance.
I don't see anyone using their pension.

15:34.683 --> 15:37.102
I'm a father now. Got to provide.

15:37.186 --> 15:39.939
So get it together and do
what you've got to do.

15:40.898 --> 15:43.233
- My wife is having a baby.
- Oh!

15:43.317 --> 15:45.653
So, we need to move
and we need to prepare.

15:46.236 --> 15:48.322
And my credit's limited from another loan.

15:48.405 --> 15:50.658
- Oh, I see.
- Yeah.

15:52.952 --> 15:55.621
Here, you can print out
everything you'll need

15:55.704 --> 15:58.207
for your application
from our website online.

15:58.290 --> 16:00.960
If you have any questions
or need assistance, just reach out.

16:01.043 --> 16:02.670
- We're here for you.
- Thanks very much.

16:03.295 --> 16:04.129
You've got this.

16:05.214 --> 16:07.049
Yes. Got it. Thank you.

16:11.261 --> 16:12.721
LOAN POLICIES AND PROCEDURES

16:24.483 --> 16:26.443
Is Lee Si-woo getting married?

16:26.527 --> 16:27.528
What?

16:28.195 --> 16:30.739
He was asking
all about getting a housing loan.

16:30.823 --> 16:32.992
- What else could it be for?
- What?

16:33.075 --> 16:35.119
So Jin Ha-kyung
will finally get her wedding?

16:35.202 --> 16:37.830
I guess. They're going fast, huh?

16:39.373 --> 16:41.917
Unless… she's pregnant?

16:42.001 --> 16:44.294
That would explain why.

16:44.378 --> 16:45.754
Yeah, it does.

16:45.838 --> 16:47.673
Oh!

16:47.756 --> 16:49.550
Huh? She's pregnant?

16:50.592 --> 16:52.177
According to the Management team.

16:52.261 --> 16:54.096
No way.

16:57.433 --> 16:59.309
One iced Americano and…

16:59.977 --> 17:02.479
- Actually, lemon tea, and that's it.
- Okay.

17:04.690 --> 17:05.941
- Director.
- Oh.

17:06.817 --> 17:08.318
You don't want coffee today?

17:08.944 --> 17:11.113
Oh, the special's lemon tea, so…

17:11.196 --> 17:14.158
- Ah.
- Oh, yeah, right. Good choice.

17:14.241 --> 17:16.410
The tea has more vitamins in it.
You'll be needing those.

17:16.493 --> 17:18.954
- Here's the citrus tea you ordered.
- Thank you.

17:19.580 --> 17:20.831
All right, I'm heading upstairs.

17:20.914 --> 17:21.957
- Yeah, okay.
- Okay.

17:23.876 --> 17:26.253
Wow, she's already
being so careful.

17:27.296 --> 17:30.215
'Cause you're not supposed
to have caffeine when you're pregnant.

17:30.299 --> 17:33.510
- Isn't that right, Mrs. Oh?
- Oh, we don't know anything for sure.

17:33.594 --> 17:35.679
Don't tell anyone else till we know.

17:35.763 --> 17:36.680
- Okay.
- See you.

17:36.764 --> 17:37.639
Mm-hmm.

17:42.227 --> 17:43.604
Hey, have you heard?

18:10.380 --> 18:11.924
Hello, everyone!

18:12.508 --> 18:15.761
These are the new candidate
during the KMA field training.

18:15.844 --> 18:18.013
We're here to observe
the forecast meeting today.

18:18.680 --> 18:20.140
Nice to meet you.

18:20.224 --> 18:22.226
- Great.
- Nice to meet you.

18:22.309 --> 18:24.436
You look so young. Nice to meet you.

18:25.104 --> 18:27.564
- All right. Let's get out of the way.
- Come on.

18:30.943 --> 18:32.861
I remember those days.

18:34.279 --> 18:36.240
Yeah? You miss it?

18:37.116 --> 18:40.869
I thought I'd do big important assignments
each and every day.

18:41.537 --> 18:43.664
And now? The magic went away?

18:44.915 --> 18:45.999
Well…

18:46.792 --> 18:48.460
It's not what I expected.

18:48.544 --> 18:50.254
I keep making mistakes.

18:50.337 --> 18:51.797
Even when I really try.

18:52.464 --> 18:53.882
If it's not what you want.

18:54.550 --> 18:56.927
Go somewhere that wants you.
You shouldn't wait it out.

18:59.721 --> 19:01.265
Why are you telling me this now?

19:03.016 --> 19:04.351
Because I know.

19:04.434 --> 19:06.812
The Policy Department
wants you to transfer.

19:08.397 --> 19:09.273
Mrs. Oh…

19:09.356 --> 19:12.025
And I know I should be asking you to stay.

19:12.609 --> 19:14.820
But I know better than anyone here

19:14.903 --> 19:18.157
that forecasting is thankless
and almost impossible.

19:18.240 --> 19:19.908
All-nighters are coming

19:19.992 --> 19:22.786
and the public still complains
even though we work so hard.

19:22.870 --> 19:25.247
I really don't want
to tell you what to do.

19:28.584 --> 19:30.544
So, think about it.

19:31.170 --> 19:33.005
You should just do what you want.

19:33.088 --> 19:34.047
Hm?

19:49.271 --> 19:51.440
Mr. Lee Myung-han, let's change your IV.

19:56.820 --> 19:59.448
It's expected to develop
as it moves over the ocean,

19:59.531 --> 20:02.993
so it should primarily affect
only the southern regions.

20:03.076 --> 20:06.496
We're expecting around 5mm
of precipitation all around the country

20:06.580 --> 20:09.082
in the weekend,
with the rain hitting Chungnam first.

20:09.166 --> 20:12.920
Please keep an on eye surface temperature
and relative humidity in our major areas.

20:13.003 --> 20:15.464
That would be all. Thank you for coming.

20:16.215 --> 20:17.090
Good work.

20:17.174 --> 20:18.967
Good work.

20:25.891 --> 20:27.517
Oh, Director Jin.

20:28.477 --> 20:30.395
- Congratulations.
- What?

20:30.479 --> 20:31.855
Congratulations for what?

20:31.939 --> 20:34.816
- I heard the good news, is it true?
- You heard good news?

20:34.900 --> 20:37.069
It's okay, we already know.

20:37.152 --> 20:39.446
- Do you have a date picked out?
- Really?

20:39.529 --> 20:42.574
Wow, we'll be invited
for a wedding dinner at least, right?

20:42.658 --> 20:44.201
Right, Director Jin?

20:44.284 --> 20:47.371
Careful he eats a ton.

20:52.167 --> 20:53.919
A wedding? For who?

20:55.420 --> 20:57.005
Wait, my father is not there right now?

20:57.089 --> 21:01.176
Yes. He-- He wasn't in his room earlier,
so we searched the building.

21:01.260 --> 21:03.303
We think he's left the hospital.

21:03.387 --> 21:04.429
He didn't contact you?

21:05.013 --> 21:05.931
No.

21:07.975 --> 21:10.811
Thank you for alerting me.
I'm sure that he must be nearby.

21:16.275 --> 21:18.277
FATHER

21:21.989 --> 21:24.366
The person you are
trying to reach is unavailable…

21:30.664 --> 21:32.541
What? From which office?

21:32.624 --> 21:36.670
Uh, it must've been from Management
when Si-woo asked about the housing loan.

21:37.379 --> 21:41.133
Si-woo's getting a housing loan,
and that means we're getting married?

21:41.883 --> 21:42.843
Well…

21:43.385 --> 21:45.637
Why else would a guy want a loan
to get a house?

21:45.721 --> 21:48.515
Plus, it's Si-woo,
who everyone knows is dating you.

21:48.598 --> 21:50.267
They connect the dots, and there you go.

21:51.560 --> 21:52.728
Still, I wish they…

21:53.937 --> 21:56.064
Why is Si-woo getting
a housing loan, then?

22:06.658 --> 22:08.702
Lee Si-woo is not at his desk?

22:08.785 --> 22:10.203
He just left, but he has his phone.

22:11.204 --> 22:12.456
So then, are you…

22:13.832 --> 22:16.043
gonna do it for real?

22:17.210 --> 22:18.420
What am I going to do?

22:18.503 --> 22:19.713
The wedding.

22:20.756 --> 22:22.883
Ah! That's ridiculous.

22:22.966 --> 22:27.095
So then, you're not pregnant,
either, are you?

22:27.179 --> 22:28.847
Why would you think that?

22:28.930 --> 22:31.183
Well, since everyone was saying
you're getting married,

22:31.266 --> 22:33.226
they thought you could be.

22:33.310 --> 22:36.396
And you had lemon tea this morning,
instead of coffee, so…

22:37.356 --> 22:38.523
Oh, the tea?

22:39.399 --> 22:40.233
Ah!

22:41.651 --> 22:45.072
Mrs. Oh. I won't have a baby anytime soon.

22:45.572 --> 22:49.493
Lee Si-woo's housing loan doesn't have
anything to do with me or us, either.

22:49.576 --> 22:53.121
So, please don't read into things.
If I have news, you'll know.

22:56.750 --> 22:57.626
In fact…

22:59.378 --> 23:01.421
There's something I need to tell you.

23:01.505 --> 23:02.923
Mr. Lee and I…

23:04.216 --> 23:05.509
stopped seeing each other

23:10.806 --> 23:13.016
Honestly, we broke up
after the last typhoon.

23:13.100 --> 23:15.310
We were worried
about what everyone would say

23:15.394 --> 23:18.897
and thought it'd be easier
to put off telling everyone, but…

23:21.274 --> 23:22.901
It just isn't working, so…

23:23.860 --> 23:26.613
Lee Si-woo and I broke up.

23:28.740 --> 23:30.534
We're sorry for not telling you sooner.

23:47.551 --> 23:48.552
You heard that?

23:50.011 --> 23:50.846
Yeah.

23:51.930 --> 23:53.765
Okay. So the act's over.

24:09.406 --> 24:11.324
So it's over for them, too.

24:16.413 --> 24:18.790
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

24:26.673 --> 24:28.550
Why were you looking at that?

24:28.633 --> 24:31.470
Eomma, you're gonna do it?

24:32.929 --> 24:34.264
Your father said it's best.

24:34.347 --> 24:36.433
I thought you were going to
give him two months.

24:37.100 --> 24:38.059
You changed your mind?

24:38.810 --> 24:40.395
Your father changed his mind.

24:40.479 --> 24:41.688
What about you?

24:42.647 --> 24:44.107
Mom, do you want a divorce?

24:52.032 --> 24:52.949
Can't you…

24:54.868 --> 24:56.536
Don't you wanna know what I think?

24:59.498 --> 25:01.666
- What are you saying?
- Don't I get an opinion?

25:01.750 --> 25:05.212
Shouldn't I get the say
whether you leave him or not?

25:05.295 --> 25:06.546
You told me to.

25:07.130 --> 25:08.840
You said to divorce him if I wanted to.

25:08.924 --> 25:11.301
I hadn't spent time with Daddy,
I didn't know.

25:12.177 --> 25:13.011
What?

25:13.094 --> 25:15.096
Now, I don't want him to go.

25:16.723 --> 25:19.267
I don't want him to go back
to living alone.

25:20.435 --> 25:21.853
So, please.

25:21.937 --> 25:23.897
Can you forget it and let him come back?

25:25.941 --> 25:28.610
You can't hate him that bad. Do you?

25:31.363 --> 25:32.614
You got school.

25:40.372 --> 25:43.041
It's between us.
We're the parents. We'll decide.

25:44.209 --> 25:45.627
Ma.

25:46.878 --> 25:48.463
Have some food and get to school.

25:53.218 --> 25:55.845
Bo-mi, you have to eat.

25:55.929 --> 25:57.222
Bring a snack.

26:10.026 --> 26:11.653
This is awful.

26:15.824 --> 26:18.910
Director Jin, I heard the good news.

26:18.994 --> 26:20.954
Uh, no. Oh no. I'm not getting married.

26:21.037 --> 26:22.122
We broke up.

26:24.833 --> 26:26.126
Director Jin--

26:26.209 --> 26:28.211
I'm not getting married. We broke up.

26:30.380 --> 26:32.090
- This is not true.
- Really?

26:37.262 --> 26:39.472
Office romance will be the death of me.

26:45.854 --> 26:48.398
- I'd like to eat alone.
- I came here to brag.

26:49.399 --> 26:51.401
Ugh, you don't know how to read the room?

26:55.530 --> 26:56.698
What is this?

26:56.781 --> 26:58.992
It's the baby. We heard the heartbeat.

26:59.868 --> 27:00.994
Wait.

27:03.455 --> 27:04.456
I saw it as well.

27:04.539 --> 27:06.958
Oh! Oh?

27:07.042 --> 27:08.418
Is it actually this loud?

27:08.501 --> 27:10.629
It was. Said the doctors.

27:12.505 --> 27:14.758
Han Ki-jun.

27:19.220 --> 27:20.972
Why do you lash out like that?

27:21.806 --> 27:23.016
Like what?

27:23.099 --> 27:26.394
You didn't have to make a big scene
dumping Si-woo with everyone there.

27:28.063 --> 27:29.314
I just told the truth.

27:29.939 --> 27:31.650
It's been over since the typhoon.

27:31.733 --> 27:33.360
Are you sure that's what he meant?

27:33.443 --> 27:34.444
What are you saying?

27:34.527 --> 27:38.031
Si-woo said all that how you
should pretend you were still together.

27:38.114 --> 27:41.117
I think it's 'cause he didn't want it
to be over between you.

27:41.701 --> 27:43.078
Which is pathetic, but…

27:43.161 --> 27:45.664
I think he just wanted to hold on to you
however he could.

27:47.332 --> 27:49.584
- Let's change the subject.
- Lee Si-woo…

27:51.670 --> 27:53.213
must still really love you.

27:58.677 --> 28:01.012
- I'm just gonna eat.
- And I think you do, too.

28:03.973 --> 28:06.434
You still have feelings for him.
I see it in your eyes.

28:14.984 --> 28:15.985
Han Ki-jun.

28:16.069 --> 28:17.153
I'm so happy for you

28:17.237 --> 28:19.531
and I need you to leave
my relationships alone.

28:19.614 --> 28:22.325
I know that I did you wrong
when I was your boyfriend,

28:22.826 --> 28:25.036
so I want to do right by you
as a friend, Ha-kyung.

28:26.371 --> 28:28.832
I'm only saying this,
'cause I'm worried about you

28:28.915 --> 28:30.500
as a friend, please.

28:31.543 --> 28:32.961
Don't just say goodbye.

28:35.463 --> 28:37.132
And I don't say it for his sake,

28:38.258 --> 28:39.259
I say it for yours.

28:41.177 --> 28:42.470
I've learned not to

28:43.805 --> 28:46.516
let the good ones get away anymore,
trust me, Ha-kyung.

28:52.105 --> 28:55.650
MOTEL
KARAOKE

29:11.541 --> 29:14.085
IMI MOTEL

29:16.629 --> 29:17.881
Let me think.

29:19.090 --> 29:21.301
Was he here? No, no, not today.

29:22.844 --> 29:25.764
- Thank you.
- Sure. Good luck.

29:28.683 --> 29:29.559
Hey.

29:29.642 --> 29:31.060
Sorry to bother you.

29:43.907 --> 29:45.492
- What? Family leave?
- Yeah.

29:45.575 --> 29:47.911
He didn't say what,
but, yeah, family thing.

29:48.536 --> 29:50.497
He wanted me to let you know
that he's off.

29:51.331 --> 29:53.625
He called Team One
and asked their Severe Weather Forecaster

29:53.708 --> 29:55.168
to come in early and cover him.

29:56.169 --> 29:57.295
Then he ran off.

29:57.378 --> 30:00.340
You don't know what's going on
with him, do you?

30:11.810 --> 30:14.896
It looks like Mr. Lee Myung-han
left the hospital this morning.

30:14.979 --> 30:17.690
What? But I thought there was more to do?
What did he say?

30:17.774 --> 30:19.984
We reached out to his son
shortly after he left.

30:20.568 --> 30:21.903
Perhaps he knew.

30:23.655 --> 30:25.573
Right, thank you. I'll give him a call.

30:49.639 --> 30:51.975
The person you are
trying to reach is unavailable.

30:52.058 --> 30:56.271
You will be connected to voicemail.
Please leave a message after the tone.

31:05.655 --> 31:06.823
Ugh!

31:06.906 --> 31:10.118
The price of that napa cabbage.
Just when I think it can't get higher.

31:10.743 --> 31:13.079
It's not worth it anymore. You can't…

31:13.162 --> 31:14.873
Oh, no. Oh, no. That's my bus, isn't it?

31:26.676 --> 31:27.760
It can't be.

31:34.267 --> 31:36.227
FATHER

31:40.607 --> 31:41.774
Hey, Dad.

31:43.860 --> 31:45.570
Dad, where did you go off to?

31:46.279 --> 31:48.031
I said where did you go?

31:52.744 --> 31:55.747
Ugh, kid, relax,
I'll go deaf listening to that.

31:58.207 --> 31:59.626
Where are you right now?

31:59.709 --> 32:01.836
That's none of your business, kid.

32:03.171 --> 32:04.464
Then what did you call for?

32:04.547 --> 32:06.299
Because I've got something to say to you.

32:08.426 --> 32:12.221
Every time I think about it,
I think you should get her back.

32:14.140 --> 32:15.975
You gotta stop being so stubborn.

32:17.477 --> 32:18.770
You can't let her slip away.

32:18.853 --> 32:19.938
Got it?

32:20.647 --> 32:21.856
You should not.

32:21.940 --> 32:24.943
You'll never gonna find another like her.
Do you understand?

32:27.070 --> 32:30.406
You got screwed over when it comes to Dad.
It's tough luck.

32:31.491 --> 32:32.659
But you got her.

32:36.120 --> 32:37.121
Hey, Dad.

32:38.331 --> 32:39.499
Where are you?

32:39.582 --> 32:42.627
You know they had more tests to do,
and the doctors said…

32:43.252 --> 32:46.172
depending on the test results,
they'll wanna do surgery.

32:46.255 --> 32:47.715
If you start chemo now--

32:47.799 --> 32:49.676
Oh, we don't need
to talk about that.

32:50.635 --> 32:52.387
It's not like I deserve your concern.

32:52.470 --> 32:54.180
So what?

32:55.807 --> 32:58.601
You still have time to be a good father
before you go.

33:01.854 --> 33:03.648
If you care about me at all,

33:03.731 --> 33:06.484
you'd leave me
with at least one good memory.

33:07.694 --> 33:09.070
'Cause I care, either way.

33:09.654 --> 33:12.782
I'm going to do everything I can
to help you, and after that,

33:13.574 --> 33:15.952
I won't cry, even if you die,
I'll stop bothering you.

33:16.619 --> 33:17.787
So, please.

33:19.330 --> 33:20.832
Get the treatment.

33:24.210 --> 33:25.837
Stay with me that long.

33:27.922 --> 33:29.382
Just until then,

33:30.174 --> 33:33.511
I want you to be like a real father.

33:35.680 --> 33:36.723
Come on, kid.

33:38.433 --> 33:40.351
Just say you want me to die.

33:42.270 --> 33:44.772
Please.

33:54.032 --> 33:55.116
Shit.

34:00.580 --> 34:01.664
Hey, kid.

34:02.248 --> 34:05.418
I know you think I'm dirt,
but I'm not all that.

34:07.295 --> 34:10.673
I care about you, I do.
Don't think I don't.

34:11.758 --> 34:13.051
All right, Dad.

34:15.887 --> 34:18.723
Nevermind.
We don't have to talk about that.

34:19.432 --> 34:21.434
I want you to get your girl back.

34:24.187 --> 34:26.189
Consider it my last wish.

34:45.541 --> 34:46.709
I'd get better, too.

34:46.793 --> 34:48.086
He has lung cancer.

34:49.754 --> 34:51.964
They like to run more tests tomorrow.

34:52.048 --> 34:55.551
If you still have to take him in,
do what you have to do.

35:13.319 --> 35:14.362
Sorry.

35:44.350 --> 35:46.686
The person you are
trying to reach is unavailable.

35:46.769 --> 35:48.646
Please leave a message after the tone.

36:27.602 --> 36:29.520
What's wrong, Tae-kyung?

36:30.188 --> 36:32.982
You wanted me to come and meet you?

36:34.984 --> 36:36.527
You've got a whole bottle.

36:42.825 --> 36:43.701
What's wrong?

36:44.744 --> 36:46.287
They said they won't do it.

36:48.039 --> 36:49.540
What are you talking about? Who?

36:50.374 --> 36:51.792
That publisher.

36:52.418 --> 36:54.503
They said my story is no good.

36:54.587 --> 36:56.380
That they can't publish it.

36:56.464 --> 36:57.381
Oh.

36:58.090 --> 36:59.717
But why?

37:00.259 --> 37:02.345
Why not? What did they say, huh?

37:02.428 --> 37:03.429
What's the reasoning?

37:04.722 --> 37:06.432
They agree with what you said.

37:07.141 --> 37:08.434
They what?

37:08.517 --> 37:11.479
What… What did they say exactly?

37:11.562 --> 37:13.773
It didn't have a hook.

37:16.901 --> 37:19.779
Anything for kids without a hook,

37:19.862 --> 37:23.532
won't stand a chance competing
with everything else.

37:29.038 --> 37:30.122
So that's it.

37:31.415 --> 37:32.875
I'm through.

37:34.126 --> 37:36.254
You're through?

37:37.296 --> 37:40.508
- Writing. Never again.
- You can't. That's ridiculous.

37:40.591 --> 37:42.969
It's not like
they're the only publishers in Korea.

37:43.552 --> 37:45.513
Yeah. It is, though.

37:46.138 --> 37:48.057
I tried everywhere else.

37:48.140 --> 37:52.311
They were the only ones
interested in working with me.

37:52.395 --> 37:54.897
I managed to ruin that too, so…

37:56.941 --> 37:59.193
Why are they all so… It's not--

38:00.653 --> 38:02.488
Oh, jeez.

38:02.571 --> 38:04.448
You can't seriously quit.

38:05.908 --> 38:08.327
Look, Seok-ho, I'm sorry.

38:08.411 --> 38:11.956
This is just what happens
to people like me.

38:12.957 --> 38:14.667
I don't have a hook.

38:15.710 --> 38:17.586
Even with my mom.

38:17.670 --> 38:21.716
That's the reason my ex-husband left, too.

38:23.092 --> 38:25.136
Listen, you don't need
a hook for me, okay?

38:25.845 --> 38:28.723
- I swear I'll never--
- You will, eventually.

38:31.058 --> 38:33.519
I start okay, then get boring.

38:34.395 --> 38:36.147
I've always been that way.

38:39.650 --> 38:43.821
Then it'll hurt a lot
when we break up like the rest.

38:50.536 --> 38:53.914
You think we're doomed?
What are you saying right now?

39:03.507 --> 39:04.842
Let's get it over with.

39:42.963 --> 39:44.965
Here. You can sit.

39:54.141 --> 39:55.101
Oh.

39:57.853 --> 40:00.231
You left so you can live like this?

40:02.024 --> 40:03.401
Why did you come all the way here?

40:07.029 --> 40:10.866
Here's some clean underwear and socks,
there are some shirts, too.

40:13.494 --> 40:15.413
Also, you're horrible, you know that?

40:16.330 --> 40:17.581
No, you're not.

40:17.665 --> 40:19.458
You're not horrible, just stupid.

40:21.544 --> 40:22.878
What are you talking about?

40:22.962 --> 40:25.297
You were the one that wanted to wait.

40:25.381 --> 40:27.883
"Just give me three months,"
that's what you said, Dong-han.

40:27.967 --> 40:29.343
And now you want out.

40:29.427 --> 40:32.847
After less than a month of trying,
you gave up and signed.

40:32.930 --> 40:35.558
If you really weren't going to try,
you shouldn't have led us on

40:35.641 --> 40:37.268
like you wanted to keep us together.

40:38.144 --> 40:41.814
I'll never be good enough for you,
no matter how much I want to.

40:43.274 --> 40:45.568
Once I realized that,
I thought I shouldn't drag things out.

40:46.527 --> 40:47.736
So I signed the papers.

40:47.820 --> 40:49.280
You don't want to commit.

40:50.781 --> 40:54.160
I did commit.
In the entirety of our marriage,

40:54.243 --> 40:56.287
I've been faithful to you as a husband.

40:56.370 --> 40:57.913
We were never your first love.

40:57.997 --> 41:00.040
- That's because you two--
- Okay.

41:00.124 --> 41:02.501
You caught me
and you called my bluff. Well done.

41:02.585 --> 41:04.545
I thought divorce papers
would scare you straight

41:04.628 --> 41:05.463
and you'd step up.

41:05.546 --> 41:07.590
I can't believe you just signed it.

41:08.257 --> 41:09.967
A real man doesn't give up.

41:10.050 --> 41:13.137
What does that say about me
who's just been waiting for you?

41:13.220 --> 41:15.181
And I don't know how you can look Bo-mi
in the eyes

41:15.264 --> 41:17.016
now that she's finally been
opening up to you.

41:17.600 --> 41:19.143
If you don't care enough to keep trying,

41:19.226 --> 41:21.729
why did you lead us on
like you were coming home finally, huh?

41:24.273 --> 41:25.733
Tell Bo-mi yourself.

41:27.026 --> 41:30.362
You can give up on us, but Bo-mi?

41:36.035 --> 41:39.538
You're a complete coward.
Do you know that? You are!

41:40.414 --> 41:42.333
Hyang-rae, I… I thought--

41:42.416 --> 41:44.627
Are you so clever
you can guess the weather,

41:44.710 --> 41:47.087
yet have no idea how your family is doing?

41:47.171 --> 41:48.422
Sorry.

41:49.089 --> 41:51.091
I'm really sorry, Hyang-rae.

41:51.175 --> 41:54.512
Enough. I'm sick of hearing you say
how sorry you are.

41:55.304 --> 41:57.890
What else can I possibly say?

41:57.973 --> 42:01.352
What's left? There's nothing for me to say
other than that I'm sorry.

42:01.936 --> 42:02.895
Try "thank you."

42:05.689 --> 42:07.733
"Thank you for waiting so long."

42:07.816 --> 42:09.777
"You were patient, thank you."

42:09.860 --> 42:12.780
You're so busy you can't eat
with your daughter on her birthday.

42:13.948 --> 42:17.243
She was so excited
that you even made a reservation.

42:17.326 --> 42:18.744
You tell her, "Thank you."

42:23.999 --> 42:26.043
Why are you so thickhead?

42:26.126 --> 42:28.087
Why are you so unaware?

42:32.341 --> 42:33.342
I'm sorry.

42:34.134 --> 42:35.386
I'm sorry.

42:38.681 --> 42:39.640
I'm sorry.

42:41.600 --> 42:42.768
Thank you, Hyang-rae.

42:46.021 --> 42:48.107
Thank you for everything.

42:48.691 --> 42:49.733
Thank you.

42:56.740 --> 42:58.867
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

43:02.913 --> 43:04.873
- Director, I have the results here.
- Okay.

43:06.709 --> 43:09.461
As expected,
there's a possibility we'll see 5mm

43:09.545 --> 43:11.338
of rain early tomorrow.

43:11.422 --> 43:13.257
I'll add that to the weekend forecast.

43:13.340 --> 43:15.384
- Yeah. Okay.
- Excuse me.

43:16.093 --> 43:18.846
We think the temperature
will drop to 3 degrees by then.

43:18.929 --> 43:19.805
It might not rain.

43:21.015 --> 43:22.433
With the current data,

43:22.516 --> 43:27.229
there's more than a 50 percent chance
the temperature will drop to one degree.

43:27.313 --> 43:30.149
That would mean, there's
an 80 percent chance of snow instead.

43:30.232 --> 43:31.442
That's what I was thinking.

43:31.525 --> 43:32.818
He's not wrong.

43:34.987 --> 43:37.031
We could recheck the precipitation data

43:37.114 --> 43:40.034
and do an analysis of the snowfall's
liquid water equivalent?

43:40.117 --> 43:41.327
How long will that take?

43:41.410 --> 43:42.995
Less than an hour, I'd say.

43:43.621 --> 43:45.748
- Let's get it started.
- Okay.

43:54.798 --> 43:56.300
She's so cool.

44:00.387 --> 44:01.722
Oh, is that so?

44:02.806 --> 44:03.891
Yes, all right.

44:06.393 --> 44:08.896
What is it? What did they say?

44:09.480 --> 44:11.398
The precipitation forecast for the weekend

44:11.482 --> 44:13.233
could actually be for snow, but we'll see.

44:13.984 --> 44:15.986
We should prepare.

44:16.070 --> 44:18.405
Oh, I got a bad feeling about this.

44:22.159 --> 44:23.118
Jeez.

44:23.827 --> 44:27.706
It could be snow or rain,
and the odds are split in half?

44:27.790 --> 44:29.083
Yes.

44:29.166 --> 44:30.918
Mm. Oh, jeez.

44:31.001 --> 44:33.921
Last time this happened,
wasn't it a huge mess?

44:34.004 --> 44:37.257
Yes. December of 2001,
the same thing happened,

44:37.341 --> 44:39.802
and we forecasted heavy snow
during evening rush hour.

44:39.885 --> 44:42.429
It wound up not getting cold enough,
so we just got rain.

44:42.513 --> 44:46.558
Criticism was so intense we had to undergo
a federal investigation.

44:47.142 --> 44:48.811
Okay, listen up.

44:49.311 --> 44:51.814
If it does turn into snow,
it's the first snow of the year.

44:52.398 --> 44:54.942
Right? That means the public and the press

44:55.025 --> 44:56.360
will watch us especially closely.

44:56.443 --> 44:57.319
Yes.

44:57.403 --> 44:58.612
Um, excuse me.

44:59.196 --> 45:00.364
It snowed already.

45:00.447 --> 45:02.700
The day before yesterday,
I saw it early in the morning.

45:02.783 --> 45:04.535
It definitely snowed
in my neighborhood.

45:04.618 --> 45:06.036
It snowed in my neighborhood, too.

45:06.120 --> 45:09.081
Yeah, uh, can someone explain it to him?

45:09.873 --> 45:11.041
- Miss Kim?
- Yes?

45:11.125 --> 45:13.502
Can you share what we mean
by the "first snow"?

45:13.585 --> 45:14.503
Oh.

45:15.921 --> 45:16.797
Okay.

45:19.425 --> 45:22.136
The official first snow
has specific criteria.

45:22.219 --> 45:24.096
We use this
for any special meteorological event,

45:24.179 --> 45:26.348
and apply them to data
from all over the country.

45:26.432 --> 45:29.143
For example, we would need someone
from the Seoul Observatory

45:29.226 --> 45:32.563
to see the snow, and then check
that it hits all the criteria

45:32.646 --> 45:34.356
to declare Seoul's first snow.

45:35.274 --> 45:37.568
Do you understand? Does that make sense?

45:37.651 --> 45:39.111
Yes.

45:39.194 --> 45:41.780
Wow, Team Two is so cool.

45:41.864 --> 45:44.158
Man, I hope I get to work at HQ.

45:44.241 --> 45:47.286
Nah, they said only the best
of the best get in here.

45:47.369 --> 45:49.997
We're all set?
Huh, enough training for today.

45:50.080 --> 45:52.875
Hm? Back to the meeting.

45:52.958 --> 45:55.753
Director Jin, your final thoughts?

45:57.087 --> 45:58.756
It's absolutely going to snow.

45:59.715 --> 46:02.176
If we put the relative humidity
at 80 percent,

46:02.259 --> 46:03.802
and the temperature is 3 degrees,

46:04.386 --> 46:07.264
there's less than a 20 percent chance
it will become snow.

46:07.347 --> 46:08.932
But if the temperature goes
down one degree,

46:09.016 --> 46:11.101
then we're at a 77 percent chance.

46:11.185 --> 46:15.022
And with the way things are now,
the odds that the temperature will drop

46:15.105 --> 46:18.484
to one degree Celcius in the next two days
is at 50 percent.

46:18.567 --> 46:20.611
True, but the temperature rose
to 6 degrees today

46:20.694 --> 46:22.654
even though it's been below zero for days.

46:22.738 --> 46:24.114
You all know that.

46:24.198 --> 46:26.742
Yes, but the air has changed drastically
since midnight yesterday.

46:26.825 --> 46:28.994
So we have less than a 50 percent chance

46:29.077 --> 46:30.829
that the temperature
will fall this evening.

46:31.622 --> 46:34.082
Can't you see how unstable
the atmosphere is now?

46:34.166 --> 46:37.085
When the sun goes down, the air
temperature will fall exponentially.

46:41.256 --> 46:43.967
Here's that analysis
you requested earlier.

46:47.513 --> 46:49.181
LIQUID WATER EQUIVALENT ANALYSIS

46:54.812 --> 46:55.938
So…

46:56.522 --> 46:57.689
Director Jin.

46:59.399 --> 47:00.526
What's your call?

47:06.532 --> 47:08.450
I wish you just tell me, sir.

47:08.534 --> 47:09.493
What?

47:09.576 --> 47:13.205
Who has the least accurate forecast
at the KMA?

47:15.332 --> 47:16.959
Oh, what?

47:17.584 --> 47:19.461
It's been ages,
you haven't put it together?

47:19.545 --> 47:21.505
I haven't and I'd really like to know.

47:21.588 --> 47:23.423
What's your secret?

47:23.507 --> 47:26.051
Your forecast are consistently right
with detailed accuracy.

47:26.134 --> 47:30.097
And I looked, they don't have records
of who got what wrong.

47:31.473 --> 47:33.267
Of course, they don't. Why would they?

47:34.768 --> 47:36.436
Want me to tell you who it is?

47:36.520 --> 47:38.689
Yes. I'd really like to know
if you're willing to share.

47:39.273 --> 47:40.107
Hm…

47:41.775 --> 47:43.819
- I am.
- What?

47:44.611 --> 47:45.445
Yeah.

47:45.529 --> 47:49.408
Oh! You can't have…
You can't be the best and the worst.

47:50.742 --> 47:52.369
I am, though, so…

47:53.704 --> 47:54.788
Hm…

47:55.706 --> 47:59.459
Over the years,
I found that getting it wrong,

48:00.043 --> 48:03.672
can often teach you more than
if you got it right the first time around.

48:06.049 --> 48:09.219
So if you learn something each instance
that you got it wrong,

48:09.303 --> 48:11.430
then one day, you'll figure it out.

48:12.014 --> 48:15.475
And your accuracy rate
goes way up over time.

48:16.894 --> 48:17.811
Makes sense?

48:18.312 --> 48:21.815
So the secret
to my record-breaking accuracy rate

48:21.899 --> 48:25.277
is simply not to focus
on how to get it right.

48:25.819 --> 48:28.113
You have to learn how not to get it wrong.

48:30.574 --> 48:33.493
Wasn't it hard getting it wrong again
so many times?

48:34.077 --> 48:37.039
It was. But no one else
keeps track of that.

48:38.790 --> 48:40.250
So how do you stop caring?

48:41.543 --> 48:43.712
You don't. You have to keep going on.

48:44.963 --> 48:47.633
I held myself accountable
for each call I made.

48:48.467 --> 48:50.594
And I knew I worked harder
than anyone else did

48:51.219 --> 48:54.139
in the hours I was deciding
those forecasts.

48:58.310 --> 48:59.394
Director Jin.

48:59.895 --> 49:01.897
What will you say in the forecast?

49:10.364 --> 49:12.449
Considering the data,
here are my thoughts.

49:12.532 --> 49:15.160
We're expecting snow after midnight.

49:15.243 --> 49:18.580
The snow will start in the west,
including the Seoul metropolitan areas.

49:18.664 --> 49:21.875
We're expecting 3 to 5cm of snow
in the central region.

49:21.959 --> 49:25.754
Oh. Can you believe the work it took
to get those three lines?

49:26.505 --> 49:28.548
It really was totally worth it.

49:30.634 --> 49:33.345
So, when are they going to transfer you?

49:35.222 --> 49:37.975
I don't know yet. Not for a while, though.

49:39.476 --> 49:40.727
What?

49:40.811 --> 49:42.729
I thought you were leaving us soon.

49:43.605 --> 49:45.732
It was looking like that
for a little while.

49:45.816 --> 49:47.776
It'd just be a waste, I thought.

49:47.859 --> 49:49.945
All the time and hard work
I put in with you,

49:50.028 --> 49:55.701
- I can't just throw that all away.
- So you're staying with us on Team Two?

49:56.243 --> 49:59.538
And I thought it was so nice
how the newbies looked up to me like that.

49:59.621 --> 50:01.957
They said HQs were the best of the best.

50:04.334 --> 50:07.796
So I'm sticking around,
at least until one of the newbies

50:07.879 --> 50:08.922
is worthy of us.

50:09.006 --> 50:14.177
Oh! You look so cute.
Look at you, that's great!

50:15.095 --> 50:19.224
Oh, I'm torn between shouting hooray
and calling you an idiot.

50:19.307 --> 50:21.226
Oh, tell me it was the right thing to do.

50:21.309 --> 50:22.644
Come on.

50:23.395 --> 50:25.063
Okay. I'm buying you dinner.

50:25.147 --> 50:26.440
What about barbecue?

50:27.983 --> 50:29.776
- I'll cover two rounds, okay?
- Yay!

50:30.861 --> 50:32.320
Oh, we can walk.

50:45.292 --> 50:47.127
Doors closing.

51:11.109 --> 51:12.569
Guess it's not here yet.

51:13.320 --> 51:14.154
No.

51:15.697 --> 51:17.032
Was this your first one?

51:17.991 --> 51:19.034
Huh?

51:20.494 --> 51:21.745
Your first snow warning.

51:23.038 --> 51:24.706
Oh, yes.

51:25.874 --> 51:29.294
Mm, it's the hardest one
to call, isn't it?

51:30.170 --> 51:31.713
Yeah.

51:34.508 --> 51:35.509
What did I say?

51:35.592 --> 51:37.969
It's just, last time,
you said localized heavy rain

51:38.053 --> 51:39.554
was the toughest forecast.

51:40.847 --> 51:45.102
Did I? Well, I'd say
it's hard if it falls from the sky.

51:45.185 --> 51:47.687
- Right?
- True.

51:48.480 --> 51:50.732
You did well. Keep going.

51:51.399 --> 51:52.484
Have a good night.

52:28.270 --> 52:30.188
I'm sorry.

52:30.272 --> 52:32.524
I was craving grapefruit so much.

52:33.066 --> 52:34.901
- Was it cold?
- No, it was fine.

52:34.985 --> 52:36.695
- Drink up, okay?
- Mm.

52:40.240 --> 52:41.324
How is it?

52:41.867 --> 52:43.368
Mmm!

52:44.077 --> 52:46.329
It's so good. I feel better.

52:46.413 --> 52:48.748
Told you. They said eat what you want.

52:49.332 --> 52:51.293
It should comfort
the morning sickness as well.

52:52.752 --> 52:54.421
Did you get that from a mommy group?

52:55.005 --> 52:56.047
Mm-hm, of course.

52:56.131 --> 52:59.176
I asked them a question online,
and they invited me right in.

52:59.259 --> 53:01.094
It's really super informative.

53:03.013 --> 53:04.014
Oh no.

53:04.097 --> 53:05.724
Who's this old lady? Where's my husband?

53:05.807 --> 53:06.933
I'd be a great old lady.

53:07.017 --> 53:09.519
- Any other cravings?
- I'm set.

53:09.603 --> 53:11.062
Okay. Should we go?

53:15.066 --> 53:16.985
Is it gonna snow in the morning?

53:17.068 --> 53:18.486
The sky is clear right now.

53:19.154 --> 53:20.739
Mm, it does.

53:20.822 --> 53:23.200
If it does, it'll be rough.

53:23.283 --> 53:25.285
If it doesn't, then we're wrong,
it's rough, too.

53:25.368 --> 53:28.496
If I got to say, it'll snow a whole lot.

53:28.580 --> 53:31.458
And everything will be covered
in white tomorrow.

53:33.460 --> 53:35.170
Doors opening.

53:36.922 --> 53:37.756
Eomma!

53:37.839 --> 53:40.425
- Doors closing.
- What are you doing here? It's so cold.

53:40.508 --> 53:42.761
Well, my daughter changed
the damn door code,

53:42.844 --> 53:44.471
so I couldn't get in.
What else could I do?

53:44.554 --> 53:47.307
Sure, I could get hypothermia,
but what else can I do?

53:48.433 --> 53:51.519
- My legs.
- You're seriously insane.

53:54.439 --> 53:55.941
Go on. Get inside.

54:17.629 --> 54:18.755
Drink this.

54:19.256 --> 54:20.924
Are you still cold?

54:23.635 --> 54:25.303
Yeah, I was frozen solid waiting for you.

54:25.387 --> 54:27.055
Are you happy now?

54:29.975 --> 54:33.895
I don't know why you keep coming over
when you know I might not be here.

54:33.979 --> 54:38.108
And stop bringing me food, too.
I almost always have to eat out.

54:39.567 --> 54:40.694
It's Si-woo again.

54:42.362 --> 54:43.655
Lee Si-woo? What did you do?

54:43.738 --> 54:45.282
Did you see him again?

54:45.365 --> 54:47.617
I heard his dad's not doing well?

54:52.622 --> 54:53.999
Si-woo said that to you?

54:56.501 --> 54:58.545
That's why he called it off, I think.

54:58.628 --> 54:59.754
To protect you.

55:03.675 --> 55:09.347
You know, that man, he's very young.
It must be very difficult.

55:11.599 --> 55:14.394
Lee Si-woo says his dad
has always made his life harder.

55:16.604 --> 55:20.358
Ah, you know better than to see an elder
as any kind of burden.

55:20.442 --> 55:22.193
That's what he is, though.

55:22.277 --> 55:24.863
You have no idea how much
he's held Si-woo back.

55:25.447 --> 55:28.325
Getting him legal trouble,
asking his son for a loan.

55:30.118 --> 55:34.581
So, you don't want to stay
with him, 'cause of that?

55:35.165 --> 55:36.374
Is it too risky?

55:37.542 --> 55:39.127
I never said I didn't want to stay.

55:39.210 --> 55:40.754
Then it works out.

55:40.837 --> 55:44.257
Your door code's even the man's birthday
for crying out loud.

55:44.799 --> 55:47.469
The door code isn't his birthday.

55:47.552 --> 55:49.554
I saw it. Don't lie to me again.

55:49.637 --> 55:51.723
Zero, three, one, four.

55:51.806 --> 55:54.517
It's not my birthday,
it's not Tae-kyung's, and it's not yours,

55:54.601 --> 55:56.811
it's not your father's, either.

55:56.895 --> 55:59.064
It's got to be his birthday, so…

56:01.066 --> 56:02.400
Don't you know the date and hour?

56:02.984 --> 56:04.778
I'm telling you the truth.

56:05.487 --> 56:07.697
Okay, ha, maybe you are compatible.

56:07.781 --> 56:09.866
I give up if you really won't admit it.

56:09.949 --> 56:11.826
It's another date.

56:13.119 --> 56:14.662
It's when we first saw each other.

56:15.330 --> 56:16.748
March 14th.

56:19.459 --> 56:22.796
We hadn't met before that,
Lee Si-woo and I.

56:28.218 --> 56:31.096
If that's what you chose
for your door code,

56:31.179 --> 56:33.014
why aren't you two together?

56:41.815 --> 56:42.649
'Cause…

56:43.858 --> 56:45.652
you can't stay together…

56:48.279 --> 56:50.156
only to avoid breaking up.

56:50.949 --> 56:52.951
He's the one that wanted it. I can't…

56:53.743 --> 56:55.912
What can I do, get on my knees and beg?

56:57.163 --> 56:58.540
And I'm his boss.

56:59.791 --> 57:01.418
It is too risky.

57:07.257 --> 57:08.383
Honestly…

57:09.092 --> 57:13.054
I've been so sad, Eomma.

57:35.452 --> 57:38.705
Want to know how ridiculous
this sounds to an outsider?

57:39.205 --> 57:41.040
"It's over 'cause we're in love."

57:41.916 --> 57:46.296
I mean, that's the dumbest most
paradoxical thing I've ever heard.

57:46.379 --> 57:48.256
It should end 'cause you're in love?

57:48.339 --> 57:50.383
What's the sense in you two breaking up?

57:50.467 --> 57:51.426
Is there any?

57:52.969 --> 57:54.846
With that, if you stay broken up,

57:55.472 --> 57:57.974
then you really
just don't love her at all.

58:02.645 --> 58:03.563
I do, though.

58:03.646 --> 58:05.732
She said the break was your idea first.

58:06.357 --> 58:07.817
It was.

58:07.901 --> 58:10.695
Only because I didn't want
to hurt at all, so…

58:10.778 --> 58:12.864
Come on. You said it first.

58:16.034 --> 58:19.454
I didn't think that she
would go for it right away.

58:19.537 --> 58:21.247
I said, "Yeah, let's break up."

58:21.915 --> 58:24.751
In reality, I'm disappointed and…

58:25.919 --> 58:27.337
really upset.

58:27.420 --> 58:31.132
Then you should've told her
you changed your mind. Why not tell her?

58:34.219 --> 58:37.555
'Cause she might have been wanting
to break up, anyway.

58:38.723 --> 58:40.642
She probably had her own reasons.

58:40.725 --> 58:42.268
Like, she could have thought,

58:43.978 --> 58:45.104
I'm too much.

58:45.855 --> 58:47.106
Oh, no.

58:47.815 --> 58:51.819
Life is far too short,
even if you're young, huh.

58:56.950 --> 58:58.159
What are you saying?

58:58.701 --> 59:01.538
Don't get caught up
worrying about the weather tomorrow.

59:01.621 --> 59:03.998
'Cause you can miss how things are today.

59:04.666 --> 59:06.501
Take a second to look up at the sky.

59:06.584 --> 59:08.795
Go to the roof, just to feel the wind.

59:08.878 --> 59:11.256
Look into the eyes of someone
that really loves you.

59:12.090 --> 59:14.092
If you can't make the most
of the current day,

59:14.175 --> 59:16.719
you don't deserve to be
worrying about tomorrow.

59:16.803 --> 59:19.013
That's why you miss things
and get it wrong.

59:19.889 --> 59:20.974
Eomma.

59:23.560 --> 59:25.645
Life is short, I know.

59:25.728 --> 59:29.399
Life is like a cloud that shoots
across the sky on a windy day.

59:29.983 --> 59:31.484
Do you follow, smarty-pants?

59:36.197 --> 59:38.741
- I'm going home.
- You're going?

59:39.325 --> 59:41.244
Don't walk me out. It's cold.

01:00:10.440 --> 01:00:12.233
"You shine brightly
when you tell me

01:00:12.317 --> 01:00:15.945
that rain needs to meet another rain
for them to get drenched."

01:00:16.988 --> 01:00:19.240
- Let it rain.
- What was that?

01:00:48.811 --> 01:00:51.773
Ugh, I'll never date
a co-worker ever again.

01:00:52.357 --> 01:00:54.859
Really? "Never" is a strong word.

01:00:55.401 --> 01:00:59.697
I know. I'm never going to date
anyone I work with, never again.

01:01:02.700 --> 01:01:07.288
But I did. I embarked
on that path again knowing the cost.

01:01:13.419 --> 01:01:14.962
Why did I do that?

01:01:52.083 --> 01:01:55.002
I like you more than anyone I've known.

01:02:25.783 --> 01:02:27.201
Forecaster Lee Si-woo, you…

01:02:29.537 --> 01:02:30.663
Jin Ha-kyung,

01:02:31.748 --> 01:02:33.082
it's always been you.

01:02:39.839 --> 01:02:41.007
Lee Si-woo.

01:02:41.924 --> 01:02:43.301
It's you.

01:03:02.069 --> 01:03:05.865
I just like you, that's all.

01:03:11.871 --> 01:03:13.748
Because I like being with you.

01:04:05.925 --> 01:04:09.512
I know we forecasted snow,
but that can change any second, right?

01:04:09.595 --> 01:04:11.430
Even if we're just getting rain instead?

01:04:11.514 --> 01:04:14.016
So watch the adiabatic chart's
vertical structure.

01:04:14.100 --> 01:04:15.393
Okay.

01:04:17.186 --> 01:04:20.439
REAL-TIME RADAR

01:05:40.144 --> 01:05:43.397
Told you. See?
It snowed after all.

01:05:54.992 --> 01:05:59.288
SEOUL OBSERVATORY

01:06:01.374 --> 01:06:02.833
What are you doing out here?

01:06:04.418 --> 01:06:06.003
I wanted to check the snow.

01:06:11.884 --> 01:06:14.762
No one really cares
about the first rain of the year.

01:06:15.471 --> 01:06:17.390
They really love the first snow, though.

01:06:18.641 --> 01:06:19.809
You know?

01:06:20.726 --> 01:06:21.978
You're right.

01:06:24.855 --> 01:06:28.192
I'll remember this snow for a long while.

01:06:30.277 --> 01:06:34.031
Like how it rained on the day
when I first met you.

01:06:35.282 --> 01:06:36.534
Do you remember?

01:06:37.284 --> 01:06:39.036
The first day we spoke to each other?

01:06:40.121 --> 01:06:43.249
Yeah, "Si-woo," "rain that comes on time."

01:06:44.125 --> 01:06:45.209
Lee Si-woo.

01:07:05.730 --> 01:07:07.940
- Fourteenth of March.
- Fourteenth of March.

01:07:13.904 --> 01:07:15.072
You know,

01:07:15.740 --> 01:07:18.325
in Spanish they have the same.

01:07:20.202 --> 01:07:24.123
"Months of sunny days would bring
a drought and then a dessert."

01:07:26.709 --> 01:07:28.252
At first, I liked that.

01:07:29.045 --> 01:07:32.006
The Lee Si-woo I knew
is so optimistic and cheerful.

01:07:34.425 --> 01:07:36.969
I was so down those days,
it was a nice change.

01:07:38.012 --> 01:07:40.681
But then, as we got to know each other,

01:07:41.390 --> 01:07:43.267
I saw your pain and learned

01:07:44.310 --> 01:07:46.979
all the things you thought
you had to hide from the world,

01:07:48.147 --> 01:07:51.901
I saw a clear picture of you.

01:07:54.111 --> 01:07:56.072
And I loved you even more for it.

01:08:02.411 --> 01:08:06.040
So I hope you won't be
too hard on yourself

01:08:06.123 --> 01:08:10.086
about that wind and the rain
you've carried with you.

01:08:13.130 --> 01:08:16.342
Wind and rain are meant to pass,
not stay forever.

01:08:19.261 --> 01:08:22.807
Everyone has their own version of a storm.

01:08:23.432 --> 01:08:27.186
And if someone's in it with you,

01:08:27.895 --> 01:08:30.815
waiting with you,
even with the rain and the wind,

01:08:32.024 --> 01:08:34.068
wouldn't you feel like it's all right?

01:08:36.362 --> 01:08:38.864
I'd like the two of us to have that.

01:08:46.789 --> 01:08:51.502
I don't just flirt around.

01:08:51.585 --> 01:08:53.420
Well, then it's good
I'm not leading you on.

01:08:55.714 --> 01:08:57.091
So let me date you.

01:08:59.343 --> 01:09:01.303
If we feel something, we date.

01:09:02.304 --> 01:09:03.722
If not, we don't.

01:09:08.018 --> 01:09:09.103
So which is it?

01:09:15.734 --> 01:09:16.735
I love you.

01:09:19.989 --> 01:09:22.199
I think I'm really in love. Is that bad?

01:09:37.673 --> 01:09:38.591
I love you.

01:09:39.175 --> 01:09:41.177
Just as much. Only more.

01:09:44.388 --> 01:09:46.348
And that love is only gonna grow.

01:09:47.600 --> 01:09:49.185
I'll love you forever.

01:10:28.974 --> 01:10:31.227
The snow looks so graceful.

01:10:34.438 --> 01:10:36.857
Think of this
when we're shoveling it tomorrow.

01:11:00.547 --> 01:11:01.799
Tae-kyung.

01:11:04.009 --> 01:11:06.804
Uh, I called, because…

01:11:06.887 --> 01:11:08.514
I looked outside,

01:11:10.516 --> 01:11:12.977
the first snow, it's so…

01:11:14.645 --> 01:11:19.441
It just looks…
It's pretty and graceful as it falls.

01:11:20.025 --> 01:11:22.945
It made me think of you.

01:11:27.283 --> 01:11:29.034
I love you so much, Tae-kyung.

01:11:32.830 --> 01:11:33.747
I…

01:11:35.791 --> 01:11:36.834
I don't want…

01:11:38.502 --> 01:11:39.837
I don't want it to be over.

01:11:41.505 --> 01:11:42.506
You're…

01:11:43.465 --> 01:11:45.050
You're my first love!

01:11:45.968 --> 01:11:47.094
I…

01:11:48.762 --> 01:11:50.723
I love you. You hear that?

01:11:51.890 --> 01:11:53.183
It's my first…

01:11:54.560 --> 01:11:57.521
I don't want to break up. Take me back.

01:12:08.073 --> 01:12:09.241
Look at that.

01:12:11.660 --> 01:12:13.454
There it is.

01:12:29.803 --> 01:12:32.306
It looks like we're getting
more snow than expected.

01:12:33.098 --> 01:12:35.225
We may need to run those numbers again.

01:12:35.309 --> 01:12:37.353
Should we get an update
on humidity report?

01:12:37.436 --> 01:12:39.104
Yeah, we should.

01:12:39.188 --> 01:12:41.440
Call Songwol-dong and ask
what's happening on their end.

01:12:41.523 --> 01:12:42.775
Okay.

01:13:07.758 --> 01:13:10.677
Chan! Gyeol! Let's go.
We need to go to school.

01:13:10.761 --> 01:13:12.763
They're already on their way. Honey.

01:13:13.389 --> 01:13:15.516
Here. Drink this and get to work.

01:13:15.599 --> 01:13:17.059
- They're gone?
- Yeah.

01:13:22.523 --> 01:13:24.858
- Thanks, honey. See you soon.
- Mm-hm

01:13:27.027 --> 01:13:28.904
- Uh, honey?
- Huh?

01:13:30.030 --> 01:13:35.035
It's… You don't have to pass the exam,
so don't think we wouldn't be fine.

01:13:35.661 --> 01:13:36.954
What are you saying?

01:13:38.497 --> 01:13:42.251
If we had to go on like this,
I love you, so we'll be good.

01:13:44.336 --> 01:13:45.587
That's all.

01:13:55.889 --> 01:13:58.684
- Hey, can I help?
- Set the table.

01:13:58.767 --> 01:13:59.852
Okay.

01:14:08.986 --> 01:14:11.071
Bo-mi, breakfast is ready.

01:14:13.490 --> 01:14:15.993
I'm not hungry. I'm going to school.

01:14:20.998 --> 01:14:22.833
What's her deal? What did I do wrong?

01:14:23.750 --> 01:14:26.295
You're fine. She found out
her boy has a girlfriend.

01:14:26.378 --> 01:14:28.755
What boy? Who is he?

01:14:29.548 --> 01:14:32.134
Relax. It's a singer from a boy band.

01:14:32.217 --> 01:14:33.760
- You can sit.
- Okay.

01:14:34.928 --> 01:14:35.888
Singer?

01:14:40.142 --> 01:14:42.436
Well, this isn't so bad.

01:14:55.741 --> 01:14:56.867
This is okay too, though.

01:14:58.410 --> 01:15:01.497
Appa, come on.
This isn't the time to laugh.

01:15:03.916 --> 01:15:04.917
Bo-mi.

01:15:05.792 --> 01:15:06.627
Are you good?

01:15:10.631 --> 01:15:11.632
I'm good.

01:15:11.715 --> 01:15:14.343
If we expect precipitation,
we have to narrow down

01:15:14.426 --> 01:15:15.677
the type we'll see.

01:15:15.761 --> 01:15:17.262
If we expect snow or sleet,

01:15:17.346 --> 01:15:20.390
then we need to figure out when it'll
all start to stick to the ground.

01:15:21.016 --> 01:15:22.809
With snow, we'll also calculate

01:15:22.893 --> 01:15:25.145
the liquid water equivalent,
and expect a snowfall as well.

01:15:25.229 --> 01:15:28.690
You're expected to know all of this
if you work at the KMA.

01:15:28.774 --> 01:15:30.400
Yes, ma'am.

01:15:30.484 --> 01:15:32.778
Who wrote the summer piece
that's on screen?

01:15:33.570 --> 01:15:34.947
"Seasonal Outlook"?

01:15:35.989 --> 01:15:36.823
I wrote it.

01:15:39.618 --> 01:15:43.705
I've told you before,
your title has to be sensational.

01:15:43.789 --> 01:15:46.166
Sensational things aren't good for kids.

01:15:47.834 --> 01:15:50.587
- You're taking your leave, right?
- Why wouldn't I? Of course, I will.

01:15:50.671 --> 01:15:52.047
When does that start?

01:15:52.130 --> 01:15:54.132
I don't know.

01:15:54.216 --> 01:15:56.218
The baby will let me know.

01:15:59.846 --> 01:16:03.559
I'll keep working until the day
this kid comes and I have to stop.

01:16:03.642 --> 01:16:05.561
You're really something.

01:16:05.644 --> 01:16:07.062
These days, I have to be.

01:16:07.729 --> 01:16:09.189
I'm a mom now.

01:16:10.983 --> 01:16:13.402
BACK IN MY DAY BY JIN TAE-KYUNG
SHIN SEOK-HO PUBLISHING COMPANY

01:16:15.445 --> 01:16:17.906
What is that?

01:16:20.117 --> 01:16:23.287
Is it? It looks like my story.

01:16:24.663 --> 01:16:25.706
Uh…

01:16:25.789 --> 01:16:29.042
There's an option to self-publish, so…

01:16:30.127 --> 01:16:31.503
I published it.

01:16:33.505 --> 01:16:35.632
Yeah, maybe there's no conventional hook,

01:16:36.341 --> 01:16:38.844
but it has lots to offer in other ways.

01:16:40.470 --> 01:16:43.265
Seok-ho.

01:16:46.059 --> 01:16:47.644
Hang on. What's that?

01:16:48.979 --> 01:16:50.564
Oh, that? Uh…

01:16:51.189 --> 01:16:54.860
I'm going to publish
all your books from now on.

01:16:55.986 --> 01:16:58.614
Oh.

01:16:59.281 --> 01:17:01.908
How did I get a guy that's so awesome?

01:17:03.118 --> 01:17:05.704
So now I just have to…

01:17:06.663 --> 01:17:11.627
keep it up until your "guy"
turns into your "husband."

01:17:13.378 --> 01:17:15.672
Uh, Tae-kyung.

01:17:21.511 --> 01:17:22.971
Uh…

01:17:23.055 --> 01:17:26.433
Okay. See you later today.

01:17:27.017 --> 01:17:28.852
- See you tonight.
- Okay.

01:17:39.613 --> 01:17:42.949
Yeah. Hey, kid,
you're gonna be late?

01:17:43.533 --> 01:17:44.910
Uh, depends on the weather.

01:17:44.993 --> 01:17:48.038
Well, even if it's a nice day,
you shouldn't leave work early.

01:17:48.121 --> 01:17:49.331
You could stay out late.

01:17:50.207 --> 01:17:53.251
Uh, you could go on a date
with your Director Lady.

01:17:53.335 --> 01:17:54.211
Huh?

01:17:54.294 --> 01:17:56.463
Don't forget your meds.

01:17:56.546 --> 01:17:59.508
And, hey, no more having all neighbors
over to play cards.

01:17:59.591 --> 01:18:01.093
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Go to work.

01:18:01.176 --> 01:18:02.761
And your chemo's in two days.

01:18:02.844 --> 01:18:06.306
I know when I have chemo.
Quit nagging. Come on.

01:18:06.390 --> 01:18:07.891
All right. See you later.

01:18:17.859 --> 01:18:19.736
Mm, if that's everyone, let's start.

01:18:21.363 --> 01:18:24.825
It is the 14th of March, 2023's
forecast meeting.

01:18:24.908 --> 01:18:26.326
Satellite Center, over to you.

01:18:26.410 --> 01:18:28.286
Yes. This is Satellite Center.

01:18:28.370 --> 01:18:31.748
Currently, we're seeing yellow dust
in the West Sea… 

01:18:31.832 --> 01:18:38.839
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

01:19:26.219 --> 01:19:27.512
I wonder

01:19:28.013 --> 01:19:32.058
if the answers in life
aren't a set constant from the start.

01:19:38.356 --> 01:19:42.861
They evolve over time and the choices
we make turn into the correct answers.

01:19:45.864 --> 01:19:50.994
So we shouldn't be afraid of making
a mistake or choosing the wrong thing.

01:19:55.457 --> 01:19:59.085
Because it still brings us closer
to the answer.

01:20:01.963 --> 01:20:04.716
I'll tell you tomorrow's forecast.

01:20:13.642 --> 01:20:14.684
Thank you.

01:20:18.939 --> 01:20:21.274
Uh, can you tell I'm nervous?

01:20:22.317 --> 01:20:24.277
Yes. It's obvious.

01:20:24.861 --> 01:20:25.987
What do I do?

01:20:26.071 --> 01:20:28.406
It's not too late.
We could abandon them and go back?

01:20:28.490 --> 01:20:31.451
No, we can't. I'm sure they've met by now.

01:20:31.535 --> 01:20:33.036
What do we do?

01:20:38.792 --> 01:20:40.585
Oh, wait a sec.

01:21:03.650 --> 01:21:04.860
What's this for?

01:21:06.069 --> 01:21:06.945
It's pretty.

01:21:10.615 --> 01:21:11.658
Let's go.

01:21:16.329 --> 01:21:18.582
Ah, it's nice to meet you.

01:21:19.165 --> 01:21:21.459
Director Jin Ha-kyung's
my youngest daughter,

01:21:21.543 --> 01:21:23.169
Bae Soo-ja. Pleasure.

01:21:23.253 --> 01:21:24.796
Uh, yes. How lovely to meet you.

01:21:25.589 --> 01:21:28.758
Of course, Lee Si-woo's my boy,
and I'm Lee Myung-han.

01:21:30.635 --> 01:21:34.014
So, tell me,
has your chemotherapy gone well?

01:21:34.097 --> 01:21:35.765
Oh, yes, yes.

01:21:36.600 --> 01:21:40.562
We'll know it worked
if I stay healthy for the next few years.

01:21:40.645 --> 01:21:41.813
Ah.

01:21:41.897 --> 01:21:45.025
I can already tell,
he's a complete moron.

01:21:45.108 --> 01:21:48.695
She's so cold she could
give a polar bear a freezer burn.

01:21:59.080 --> 01:22:01.583
Should we just go?

01:22:03.919 --> 01:22:04.794
Let's do it.
